{"speciesId":548,"names":{"fr":"Chlorobule","es":"Petilil","en":"Petilil","ja":"チュリネ"},"descriptions":[{"language":"fr","version":"black","text":"Les feuilles sur sa tête sont très amères, mais elles remettent d’aplomb les corps les plus éreintés."},{"language":"en","version":"black","text":"The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body."},{"language":"fr","version":"white","text":"Il aime les zones bien irriguées et riches en nutriments. On sait que là où il vit, les cultures sont florissantes."},{"language":"en","version":"white","text":"Since they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants."},{"language":"en","version":"black-2","text":"The leaves on its head grow right back even if they fall out. These bitter leaves refresh those who eat them."},{"language":"en","version":"white-2","text":"The leaves on its head grow right back even if they fall out. These bitter leaves refresh those who eat them."},{"language":"fr","version":"x","text":"Les feuilles sur sa tête sont très amères, mais elles remettent d’aplomb les corps les plus éreintés."},{"language":"es","version":"x","text":"Mordisquear las hojas de su cabeza permite recuperar toda la vitalidad, a pesar de que están muy amargas."},{"language":"en","version":"x","text":"The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body."},{"language":"ja","version":"x","text":"頭の 葉っぱを かじると とても 苦いが 疲れた 体を 元気にする 効果が あるのだ。"},{"language":"fr","version":"y","text":"Il aime les zones bien irriguées et riches en nutriments. On sait que là où il vit, les cultures sont florissantes."},{"language":"es","version":"y","text":"Habita tierras húmedas ricas en nutrientes donde la cosecha es abundante."},{"language":"en","version":"y","text":"Since they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants."},{"language":"ja","version":"y","text":"水分と 栄養の 豊富な 土を 好むので チュリネの 住む 土地は 作物の 育ちが 良い。"},{"language":"fr","version":"omega-ruby","text":"Les feuilles sur sa tête sont très amères, mais elles remettent d’aplomb les corps les plus éreintés."},{"language":"es","version":"omega-ruby","text":"Mordisquear las hojas de su cabeza permite recuperar toda la vitalidad, a pesar de que están muy amargas."},{"language":"en","version":"omega-ruby","text":"The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body."},{"language":"ja","version":"omega-ruby","text":"頭の 葉っぱを かじると とても 苦いが 疲れた 体を 元気にする 効果が あるのだ。"},{"language":"fr","version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Il aime les zones bien irriguées et riches en nutriments. On sait que là où il vit, les cultures sont florissantes."},{"language":"es","version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Habita tierras húmedas ricas en nutrientes donde la cosecha es abundante."},{"language":"en","version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Since they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants."},{"language":"ja","version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"水分と 栄養の 豊富な 土を 好むので チュリネの 住む 土地は 作物の 育ちが 良い。"},{"language":"fr","version":"sun","text":"Les feuilles sur sa tête sont amères à en cracher ses papilles, mais peuvent requinquer les corps les plus meurtris, surtout en infusion."},{"language":"es","version":"sun","text":"Las hojas de su cabeza son tan amargas que casi producen náuseas, pero tienen un efecto revitalizante, sobre todo en forma de infusión."},{"language":"en","version":"sun","text":"Although the leaves on its head are bitter enough to cause dizziness, they provide relief from weariness—even more so when boiled."},{"language":"ja","version":"sun","text":"頭の葉っぱは めまいが するほど 苦いが 疲れた 身体に 効く。 煎じて 飲めば もっと 効く。"},{"language":"fr","version":"moon","text":"Il est recommandé de tailler de temps à autre les feuilles de Chlorobule afin qu’il acquière une forme parfaitement ronde et harmonieuse."},{"language":"es","version":"moon","text":"Adquiere un aspecto esplendoroso cuando se le recortan las hojas de la cabeza con cierta asiduidad."},{"language":"en","version":"moon","text":"By pruning the leaves on its head with regularity, this Pokémon can be grown into a fine plump shape."},{"language":"ja","version":"moon","text":"たまに 葉っぱを トリミングすると 丸々とした 立派な 姿に 育って いくのだ。"},{"language":"fr","version":"ultra-sun","text":"En raison de leurs vertus revigorantes, les feuilles de sa tête sont séchées au soleil puis bues en infusion par les personnes âgées."},{"language":"es","version":"ultra-sun","text":"Los ancianos aprecian las hojas de su cabeza, ya que, secadas al sol y tomadas en infusión, devuelven la vitalidad perdida."},{"language":"en","version":"ultra-sun","text":"Some say if you dry the leaves on its head, boil them down, and drink the infusion, your vigor will return, so Petilil is popular with the elderly."},{"language":"ja","version":"ultra-sun","text":"頭の 葉を 天日で 乾かし 煎じて 飲むと 当時の 元気が 戻ると お年寄りに 大人気。"},{"language":"fr","version":"ultra-moon","text":"À cheval sur la qualité de la terre et de l’eau, il migre avec ses congénères lorsque son environnement se dégrade."},{"language":"es","version":"ultra-moon","text":"Prefiere el agua y la tierra sin impurezas. Si el entorno en el que habita empeora, emigra en grupo hacia un nuevo territorio."},{"language":"en","version":"ultra-moon","text":"They prefer clean water and soil. When the environment they live in turns bad, the whole bunch will up and move to a new area."},{"language":"ja","version":"ultra-moon","text":"綺麗な 水と 土を 好む。 棲み処の 環境が 悪くなると 新たな土地へと 群れで 引っ越す。"},{"language":"fr","version":"sword","text":"Il apparaît non loin des eaux propres. On utilise parfois les infusions préparées avec les feuilles de sa tête pour éloigner les insectes."},{"language":"es","version":"sword","text":"Aparece en lugares de aguas limpias. La decocción de las hojas de su cabeza se puede utilizar como repelente de insectos."},{"language":"en","version":"sword","text":"Petilil appears around sources of clean water. Boiling leaves from this Pokémon’s head results in a liquid that’s sometimes used as a bug repellent."},{"language":"ja","version":"sword","text":"きれいな 水辺に 現れる。 頭の 葉を 煮だした 汁は 虫よけに 使われることもある。"},{"language":"fr","version":"shield","text":"Plus ses feuilles sont foncées, plus il est en bonne santé. Il s’installe parfois dans les champs ou les parterres de fleurs bien entretenus."},{"language":"es","version":"shield","text":"Cuanto más sano está este Pokémon, más intenso se vuelve el color de sus hojas. A veces se asienta en huertos o jardines de flores bien cuidados."},{"language":"en","version":"shield","text":"The deeper the color of a Petilil’s leaves, the healthier the Pokémon is. Petilil sometimes makes its home in a well-tended field or flowerbed."},{"language":"ja","version":"shield","text":"葉の 色が 濃いほど 健康。 手入れの 行き届いた 畑や 花壇に 棲みつくことも ある。"},{"language":"en","version":"legends-arceus","text":"The leaves on its head are highly valued for medicinal purposes. Dry the leaves in the sun, boil them, and then drink the bitter decoction for remarkably effective relief from fatigue."}],"varieties":[{"id":548,"moves":[{"name":"cut","learns":[[11,"machine",0],[14,"machine",0],[15,"machine",0],[16,"machine",0]]},{"name":"absorb","learns":[[11,"level-up",1],[14,"level-up",1],[15,"level-up",1],[16,"level-up",1],[17,"level-up",1],[18,"level-up",1],[20,"level-up",1],[24,"level-up",1],[25,"level-up",1]]},{"name":"mega-drain","learns":[[11,"level-up",13],[14,"level-up",13],[15,"level-up",13],[16,"level-up",13],[17,"level-up",13],[18,"level-up",13],[20,"level-up",9],[25,"level-up",9]]},{"name":"leech-seed","learns":[[11,"level-up",8],[14,"level-up",8],[15,"level-up",8],[16,"level-up",8],[17,"level-up",8],[18,"level-up",8],[20,"level-up",24],[25,"level-up",24]]},{"name":"growth","learns":[[11,"level-up",4],[14,"level-up",4],[15,"level-up",4],[16,"level-up",4],[17,"level-up",4],[18,"level-up",4],[20,"level-up",1],[25,"